rooms_desc ({"This is the parlor of Cavalier's humble home.  This is the room in which heholds general conversations with friends and visitors.  This also the roomin which he holds his parties.  Along the east side of the room, there isa large black velvet futon chair.  To the right of that there sits a large over-stuffed chair covered in the like.  In the middle of theroom sits a large, but sturdy coffee table.  Along the west side ofthe room sits a large, comfortable, black leather couch.  It looks VERYinviting.  On both ends of the couch, there sits large sturdy end tableswhich match the coffee table.  Along the north wall sits a large e      entertainment center whcih features a multi-disc CD changer and bigscreen tv.  It also contains a large number of cd racks, filled with Kansas, Queen, Clannad, Enya, U2, Midnight Oil and other spectacular groups.  This system also features two 5 foot Infinity tower speakers and various amps.  The floor is covered by afabulously plush, light blue, shag carpet that looks inviting enough tolie down and sleep on, along with other various activities.  It looksvery expensive.  From the ceiling there are various hanging plants,consisting mainly of ivys.  Over all, this is a very inviting room.","This is a brand new, unfurnished room.  As soon as you see it, youstart imagining interesting ways to decorate it.. it could be anything,a cupboard, a conservatory, an orchard, heaven or hell..A small note in the corner says:  'help build/furnish'.","This is Cavalier's master bedroom.  It is very tastefully decoratedwith very masterful reproductions of such classic artworks as the MonaLisa, as well as other works by the Masters.  The center of the room isdominated by a super king water bed, which is covered by black silk sheetsand comforters.  The floor is again covered by a VERY inviting, super-plushshag carpet.  However, despite the obvious comforts of this room, there isa sadness about it.  It's as if something, or someone, who once gracedthis room is now gone.  Not only from the room, but from Cavalier's life.It is almost an uncomfortable, saddening feeling that would proably distress most visitors to this room.",0,0,0,0,0,0,0,})
